#3503
innkeeper~
the Innkeeper~
The Innkeeper stands here, cleaning glasses.
~
The Innkeeper now spends most of his days waiting for customers, while the
nights are spent watching out for goblins.  His inn is no longer the happy
place that is used to be in days past.
~
67 0 0 S
10 8 1 1d12+200 2d8+1
1500 0
0 0 1
>speech_prog rest room inn drink rumor goblin road~
mpecho The Innkeeper polishes a glass and says 'Goblins on the high road, wyverns over it. Rest while you still have a here to rest in.'
~
>speech_prog sleep food tavern~
if rand(14)
mpecho $I says 'Rest before the road. The road never rests before you.'
else
if rand(17)
mpecho $I says 'Drink, sleep, or leave. Bleeding on the floor is none of those.'
else
if rand(20)
mpecho $I says 'Heroes who forget to stand up before walking out die in my doorway. Don't.'
else
if rand(25)
mpecho $I says 'The stew is brown. Don't ask what kind of brown. The brave don't ask.'
else
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'Room's upstairs, ale's downstairs, regret's wherever you left it. Enjoy your stay.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I says 'I've heard every adventurer's life story twice. Tip well and I'll pretend yours is new.'
else
mpecho $I polishes a mug that was clean an hour ago and will be clean an hour from now.
endif
endif
endif
endif
endif
endif
~
