#3504
bard~
the bard~
A sullen bard is here, drinking away his problems.
~
You can smell the alcohol on his breath from across the room.  This poor bard
has been sitting here quite a while, drinking himself into oblivion.
~
67 8 0 S
8 13 3 1d12+110 2d6+0
1500 0
0 0 1
>speech_prog song bard rumor goblin dark horseman drink~
if rand(50)
mpecho The sullen bard says 'I'd sing of glory, but the goblins keep editing my audience.'
else
mpecho The sullen bard says 'There's a horseman who rides the dark roads. Don't flag him down. He stops for the wrong people.'
endif
~
>speech_prog gossip hero boss treasure~
if rand(14)
mpecho $I says 'Every treasure has an owner. Every owner has teeth.'
else
if rand(17)
mpecho $I says 'Ask around enough and even idiots become a map.'
else
if rand(20)
mpecho $I sings 'Heroes are just survivors with better press.'
else
if rand(25)
mpecho $I says 'I'd tell you the rumor, but rumors are like ale — first round's the only honest one.'
else
if rand(33)
mpecho $I says 'They say the boss has a weakness. They always say that. Sometimes they're even alive to say it.'
else
if rand(50)
mpecho $I leans in. 'I heard a thing. It's probably a lie. The best ones usually are.'
else
mpecho $I says 'A song about your deeds? Sure. I'll need to know you survived them first. Awkward, I know.'
endif
endif
endif
endif
endif
endif
~
